{"text": "WAR AND LAW: CHILCOT\u2019S IRAQI LESSONS AND IRANIAN CHALLENGES\n\nThe Annual 80 Club Lecture is organised by Liberal Democrat Lawyers'\n\nAssociation in association with CentreForum\n\nTuesday 14th December 2010, 6 p.m.\nNational Liberal Club\n\nPhilippe Sands OC'\n\nBaroness Falkner, Ladies and Gentlemen, I begin by thanking the Liberal Democrat\nLawyer\u2019s Association for inviting me to deliver the Annual 80 Club Lecture, and also for\nthe support provided by CentreForum.\nLast September, the respected American commentator Jeffrey Goldberg, writing in the\nmonthly magazine The Atlantic, imagined different scenarios responding to the prospect\nof a nuclearised Iran.\u2019 \u201cIt is possible\u201d, he wrote, \u201cthat at some point in the next 12\nmonths, the imposition of devastating economic sanctions on the Islamic Republic of Iran\nwill persuade its leaders to cease their pursuit of nuclear weapons\u201d, or that \u201cIran\u2019s\nreform-minded Green Movement will somehow replace the mullah-led regime\u201d, or that\n\u201cfoiling operations\u2019 conducted by the intelligence agencies of Israel, the United States,\n\nGreat Britain, and other Western powers ... will have hindered Iran\u2019s progress in some\n\n' Professor of Law, University College London; Barrister, Matrix Chambers. I would like to thank Rabinder\nSingh QC for his characteristically insightful and pertinent observations, and Ioana Hyde for research\nassistance.\n> Jeffrey Goldberg, \u2018The Point of No Return\u2019, http://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/1969/12/the-\npoint-of-no-return/8186/",
